title: Bedrock model access enabled
name: jackproof_bedrock_model_enablement
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_model_enablement"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal requested access to a Bedrock foundation model. Field and event names follow the CloudTrail documentation and have not been checked against a live tenant.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventSource: bedrock.amazonaws.com
    eventName:
      - PutFoundationModelEntitlement
      - CreateFoundationModelAgreement
  condition: selection
level: medium
tags:
  - attack.impact
  - attack.t1496
falsepositives:
  - Planned enablement of a model in an account that is meant to use models
---
title: Bedrock model invocation
name: jackproof_bedrock_invocation
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_invocation"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal invoked a Bedrock model. This rule is a building block for the correlation rules and is not meant to alert on its own.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventSource: bedrock.amazonaws.com
    eventName:
      - InvokeModel
      - InvokeModelWithResponseStream
      - Converse
      - ConverseStream
  condition: selection
level: informational
---
title: Bedrock streaming model invocation
name: jackproof_bedrock_streaming_invocation
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_streaming_invocation"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal invoked a Bedrock model with a streaming response. This rule is a building block for the streaming burst correlation.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventSource: bedrock.amazonaws.com
    eventName:
      - InvokeModelWithResponseStream
      - ConverseStream
  condition: selection
level: informational
---
title: Bedrock model listing or availability check
name: jackproof_bedrock_model_listing
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_model_listing"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal listed Bedrock models or checked availability. This rule is a building block for the reconnaissance correlation.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventSource: bedrock.amazonaws.com
    eventName:
      - ListFoundationModels
      - GetFoundationModel
      - ListInferenceProfiles
  condition: selection
level: informational
---
title: Bedrock invocation logging configuration read
name: jackproof_bedrock_logging_read
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_logging_read"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal read the Bedrock model invocation logging configuration. This rule is a building block for the logging removal correlation.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventSource: bedrock.amazonaws.com
    eventName: GetModelInvocationLoggingConfiguration
  condition: selection
level: informational
---
title: Bedrock invocation logging configuration deleted
name: jackproof_bedrock_logging_deleted
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_logging_deleted"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal deleted the Bedrock model invocation logging configuration. Deleting it removes the record of what models were called.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventSource: bedrock.amazonaws.com
    eventName: DeleteModelInvocationLoggingConfiguration
  condition: selection
level: high
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.t1562
falsepositives:
  - A planned change of the logging destination
---
title: IAM access key created
name: jackproof_access_key_created
id: {{uuid "jackproof_access_key_created"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal created an IAM access key. This rule is a building block for the key created and used correlation.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventSource: iam.amazonaws.com
    eventName: CreateAccessKey
  condition: selection
level: informational
---
title: Request signed with an access key
name: jackproof_access_key_used
id: {{uuid "jackproof_access_key_used"}}
status: experimental
description: Any AWS API request signed with an access key. This rule is a building block for the key created and used correlation.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventSource|endswith: .amazonaws.com
  filter:
    userIdentity.accessKeyId: null
  condition: selection and not filter
level: informational
---
title: Vertex AI or Gemini API enabled in a project
name: jackproof_gcp_model_service_enabled
id: {{uuid "jackproof_gcp_model_service_enabled"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal enabled the Vertex AI or Gemini API service in a project. Field and method names follow the Cloud Audit Logs documentation and have not been checked against a live project.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: gcp
  service: gcp.audit
detection:
  selection:
    protoPayload.serviceName: serviceusage.googleapis.com
    protoPayload.methodName|endswith:
      - EnableService
      - BatchEnableServices
    protoPayload.resourceName|contains:
      - aiplatform.googleapis.com
      - generativelanguage.googleapis.com
  condition: selection
level: medium
tags:
  - attack.impact
  - attack.t1496
falsepositives:
  - Planned enablement of a model service in a project that is meant to use models
---
title: Azure OpenAI account or deployment written
name: jackproof_azure_openai_written
id: {{uuid "jackproof_azure_openai_written"}}
status: experimental
description: A principal created or changed an Azure OpenAI account or deployment. Field and operation names follow the Activity Log documentation and have not been checked against a live subscription.
author: jackproof
logsource:
  product: azure
  service: activitylogs
detection:
  selection:
    operationName:
      - MICROSOFT.COGNITIVESERVICES/ACCOUNTS/WRITE
      - MICROSOFT.COGNITIVESERVICES/ACCOUNTS/DEPLOYMENTS/WRITE
  condition: selection
level: medium
tags:
  - attack.impact
  - attack.t1496
falsepositives:
  - Planned creation of an Azure OpenAI account
---
title: Bedrock model enabled and then invoked by the same principal
name: jackproof_bedrock_enable_then_invoke
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_enable_then_invoke"}}
status: experimental
description: Corresponds to JP-HUNT-001.
author: jackproof
correlation:
  type: temporal_ordered
  rules:
    - jackproof_bedrock_model_enablement
    - jackproof_bedrock_invocation
  group-by:
    - userIdentity.arn
  timespan: {{.EnableThenInvokeWindow}}
level: high
---
title: Bedrock invocation volume above a fixed floor
name: jackproof_bedrock_volume
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_volume"}}
status: experimental
description: Corresponds to JP-HUNT-002. Sigma cannot express a rolling median baseline, so this rule uses the fixed request floor from min_requests. Use the jackproof hunt command for the baseline comparison.
author: jackproof
correlation:
  type: event_count
  rules:
    - jackproof_bedrock_invocation
  group-by:
    - userIdentity.arn
  timespan: {{.VolumePeriod}}
  condition:
    gte: {{.MinRequests}}
level: medium
---
title: Bedrock invocations from many source addresses
name: jackproof_bedrock_many_source_addresses
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_many_source_addresses"}}
status: experimental
description: Corresponds to the many addresses check of JP-HUNT-004.
author: jackproof
correlation:
  type: value_count
  rules:
    - jackproof_bedrock_invocation
  group-by:
    - userIdentity.arn
  timespan: {{.DistinctIPWindow}}
  condition:
    gte: {{.DistinctIPs}}
    field: sourceIPAddress
level: high
---
title: Access key created and then used
name: jackproof_access_key_created_then_used
id: {{uuid "jackproof_access_key_created_then_used"}}
status: experimental
description: Corresponds to JP-HUNT-005. The correlation joins the created key with the key that signs later requests. Comparing the source address of the two events is left to the analyst.
author: jackproof
correlation:
  type: temporal_ordered
  rules:
    - jackproof_access_key_created
    - jackproof_access_key_used
  group-by:
    - access_key
  aliases:
    access_key:
      jackproof_access_key_created: responseElements.accessKey.accessKeyId
      jackproof_access_key_used: userIdentity.accessKeyId
  timespan: {{.KeyUseWindow}}
level: high
---
title: Bedrock model listing followed by invocation
name: jackproof_bedrock_recon_then_invoke
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_recon_then_invoke"}}
status: experimental
description: Corresponds to the listing check of JP-HUNT-006. Whether the invocation is the principal's first is left to the analyst.
author: jackproof
correlation:
  type: temporal_ordered
  rules:
    - jackproof_bedrock_model_listing
    - jackproof_bedrock_invocation
  group-by:
    - userIdentity.arn
  timespan: {{.ReconWindow}}
level: medium
---
title: Bedrock invocation logging configuration read and then deleted
name: jackproof_bedrock_logging_read_then_deleted
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_logging_read_then_deleted"}}
status: experimental
description: Corresponds to the logging removal check of JP-HUNT-006.
author: jackproof
correlation:
  type: temporal_ordered
  rules:
    - jackproof_bedrock_logging_read
    - jackproof_bedrock_logging_deleted
  group-by:
    - userIdentity.arn
  timespan: {{.ReconWindow}}
level: high
---
title: Burst of Bedrock streaming invocations
name: jackproof_bedrock_streaming_burst
id: {{uuid "jackproof_bedrock_streaming_burst"}}
status: experimental
description: Corresponds to JP-HUNT-008. Sigma cannot test that the requests use uniform parameters, so this rule counts streaming requests only.
author: jackproof
correlation:
  type: event_count
  rules:
    - jackproof_bedrock_streaming_invocation
  group-by:
    - userIdentity.arn
  timespan: {{.StreamWindow}}
  condition:
    gte: {{.StreamConcurrency}}
level: high
